.TH UDBACHK 8 "May 10 1999 - version 0.11"
.SH NAME
udbachk \- passwd, group, shadow and gshadow file integrity checker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B udbachk
[-d] [-p path] [-g path] [-s path] [-G path] [-f file] [-v] [-h]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This program checks passwd, group, shadow and gshadow file integrity. The
program does not do anything else but reports possible problems with the
files and their states.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I "\-d, \-\-default"
Check files /etc/passwd /etc/group /etc/shadow and /etc/gshadow
.TP
.I "\-p, \-\-passwd"
Path to the passwd file which you want to check.
.TP
.I "\-g, \-\-group"
Path to the group file which you want to check.
.TP
.I "\-s, \-\-shadow"
Path to the shadow file which you want to check.
.TP
.I "\-G, \-\-gshadow"
Path to the gshadow file you want to check.
.TP
.I "\-f, \-\-file"
Write output to a file instead of the standard output.
.TP
.I "\-v, \-\-version"
Print version information to standard output and exit successfully.
.TP
.I "\-h, \-\-help"
Print help to standard output and exit successfully.
.SH FILES
.if n .ta 2.8i
.if t .ta 2.1i
$HOME/.udbachk.conf	overrides system defaults
.br
/usr/local/etc/udbachk.conf	system defaults
.PP
There can be following definitions in configuration file. White spaces 
and empty lines are ignored. Character for commentation is # (hash).
.TP
PATH_TO_PASSWD
Path to the passwd file. If not defined, no check will be made.
.TP
PATH_TO_GROUP
Path to the group file. If not defined, no check will be made.
.TP
PATH_TO_SHADOW
Path to the shadow file. If not defined no, check will be made.
.TP
PATH_TO_GSHADOW
Path to the shadow group file. If not defined, no check will be made
.TP
MODE_FOR_PASSWD
passwd file mode. If any of the numbers is 8 or 9 no check will be made for
that permission and right permission is taken to be zero. Notice that
permission is not an umask. It is numeric mode which is used with chmod.
.TP
MODE_FOR_GROUP
group file mode. See mode for passwd.
.TP
MODE_FOR_SHADOW
shadow file mode. See mode for passwd.
.TP
MODE_FOR_GSHADOW
gshadow file mode. See mode for passwd.
.TP
LONGEST_LOGIN_NAME
Longest allowed login name which does not cause a warning.
.TP
LONGEST_GROUP_NAME
Longest allowed group name which does not cause a warning.
.TP
MIN_UID
Smallest allowed UID that does not cause a warning.
.TP
MAX_UID
Biggest allowed UID that does not cause a warning.
.TP
MIN_GID
Smallest allowed GID that does not cause a warning.
.TP
MAX_GID
Biggest allowed GID that does not cause a warning.
.SH BUGS
Program outputs too much irrelevant stuff.
.SH AUTHOR
Sami Kerola <kerolasa@iki.fi>
.SH "SEE ALSO"
